WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.492
Next semester, your machine learning course will go much deeper.

00:00:04.492 --> 00:00:14.802
You may study linear and logistic regression in more detail, followed by decision trees, random forests,

00:00:14.802 --> 00:00:23.527
support vector machines, nearest-neighbor methods, cross-validation, model tuning, feature engineering, class imbalance,

00:00:23.527 --> 00:00:28.111
clustering, neural networks, and other predictive methods.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:31.908
You do not need to memorize all of those algorithms now.

00:00:31.908 --> 00:00:35.693
The important foundation is already in place.

00:00:35.693 --> 00:00:43.608
You understand that observations become feature vectors, many feature vectors form X, targets form y,

00:00:43.608 --> 00:00:52.413
training estimates model parameters, test data evaluates generalization, and metrics help us understand performance.

00:00:52.413 --> 00:00:59.553
You also understand that leakage, data quality, and interpretation matter as much as calling fit and predict.

00:00:59.553 --> 00:01:07.533
That foundation will make the next course easier to follow because the algorithms will fit into a workflow that you

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:09.584
already understand.
